{
    private static string Html(string data) => """
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Learning which evidence to request · Gojo</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#eeeee2;color:#27454a;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1420px;margin:auto;padding:35px 24px 70px}header{max-width:1100px}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;line-height:1.2}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,49px);margin:12px 0 20px}h2{font-size:30px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.13em;color:#a96640;font-weight:700}.lede{font-size:19px}a{color:#246a70;text-underline-offset:3px}.nav{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:20px 0}.nav a{padding:6px 13px;border:1px solid #d5d5c6;border-radius:20px;background:#fbf8ef;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px}.note,.costs{background:#e1e6d9;border-left:3px solid #849465;padding:15px 20px;margin:24px 0}.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{padding:10px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #d5d5c6;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{font-weight:650}tr.learned{background:#e1e6d9}section{margin:35px 0}article{background:#fbf8ef;border:1px solid #d5d5c6;padding:22px;margin:24px 0;scroll-margin-top:20px}h3{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:20px}.meta{font-size:14px;color:#617269}.pictures{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}figure{margin:10px 0;min-width:0}img{width:100%;height:130px;object-fit:cover;display:block}figcaption{font-size:14px}.empty{height:130px;display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;border:1px dashed #b5b5a4;background:#f0eee3;padding:20px}.status{padding:10px 14px;background:#e6eddf;border-left:3px solid #638068;margin:14px 0}.status.open{background:#f1e6d5;border-color:#b9803f}.steps{counter-reset:step;display:grid;gap:10px;margin-top:15px}.step{border-left:3px solid #8aa5a4;padding:10px 14px;background:#f0f0e6}.step h4{margin:0;font-size:15px}.step p{font-size:14px;margin:5px 0}.step code{font-size:13px;color:#795439}.small{font-size:14px}details{border-top:1px solid #d5d5c6;padding:15px 0}summary{cursor:pointer}.footer{font-size:14px;border-top:1px solid #d5d5c6;margin-top:30px;padding-top:20px}pre{overflow:auto;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px}@media(max-width:800px){main{padding:25px 14px}.pictures{grid-template-columns:1fr}article{padding:16px}th,td{padding:8px}}
</style></head><body><main>
<header><span class="eyebrow">Gojo · bounded learned evidence selection</span><h1>Learn which question to ask.<br>Keep the answer in the structure.</h1>
<p class="lede">A small CPU policy learns from the outcomes of requesting exposed span evidence. Native hypotheses, publications and compatibility readers still decide what the evidence supports.</p>
<p>The policy receives actual advertised roles and competing proposals. Concealed source words are available only through a requested port. Training and evaluation use different layout families within the same finite four-edge-cell vocabulary.</p>
<nav class="nav"><a href="diagnostics.json">Run data</a><a href="evidence.gojo.json.gz">Retained native witnesses</a><a href="local-costs.json">Local execution cost probe</a><a href="../equivalence-revision/gallery.html">Earlier revision cases</a></nav></header>
<div class="note"><strong>What is learned?</strong> Five coefficients rank the next available evidence port using structural disagreement, query overlap, offered roles and previously published participation. A learned score cannot override native compatibility, manufacture missing evidence or settle conflicting suppliers.</div>
<section><h2>Held-out layout families</h2><p id="run" class="small"></p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Selection policy</th><th>Episodes</th><th>Correctly identified</th><th>Still open</th><th>Mean requests</th></tr></thead><tbody id="summary"></tbody></table></div><p class="small">Every policy sees the same finite candidates and exposed services. The fixed baseline visits all vertical services first, deliberately wasting requests where the candidates agree. The disagreement baseline is the stronger comparison. Identification concerns this declared library, not all possible source structures.</p></section>
<section><h2>Learned read and measured cost</h2><div id="training"></div><div id="costs" class="costs"></div><p class="small">Elapsed time covers this local training/evaluation pass, excluding SDK build, browser rendering and archive capture. Allocated bytes measure cumulative managed allocation, not live RAM. The separate local cost probe measures full native capture and restoration.</p></section>
<section><h2>Inspect selected episodes</h2><p>These pictures execute fresh native outputs after evidence selection. They are illustrative realizations, not inputs to the policy. Source observations, candidate proposals and actual sampled output remain separate.</p><div id="episodes"></div></section>
<details><summary>Scope, controls and interpretation</summary><ul id="limits"></ul></details>
<footer class="footer"><p id="archive"></p><p>The policy is a small ridge-regression read of retained native training outcomes. This is genuine parameter fitting, but it is not a trained ornament recognizer, a general hypothesis generator or a neural foundation model.</p></footer>
<script id="data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script><script>
'use strict';const model=JSON.parse(document.querySelector('#data').textContent),esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const names={fixed:'Fixed port order',random:'Seeded random',disagreement:'Structural disagreement',learned:'Learned ranking'};
document.querySelector('#run').textContent=`${model.options.trainingEpisodes} training episodes · ${model.options.evaluationEpisodes} held-out episodes per policy · ${model.options.maxRequests} requests maximum · seed ${model.options.seed}.`;
document.querySelector('#summary').innerHTML=model.summaries.map(s=>`<tr class="${s.policy==='learned'?'learned':''}"><td>${esc(names[s.policy]||s.policy)}</td><td>${s.episodes}</td><td>${s.identified}</td><td>${s.open}</td><td>${s.meanRequests.toFixed(2)}</td></tr>`).join('');
document.querySelector('#training').innerHTML=`<p>${model.training.rows} acquired training outcomes support the native policy surface. No held-out source words enter fitting.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Derived feature</th><th>Learned coefficient</th></tr></thead><tbody>${model.training.features.map((f,i)=>`<tr><td>${esc(f)}</td><td>${model.training.coefficients[i].toFixed(4)}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div>`;
document.querySelector('#costs').textContent=`Local training + evaluation: ${(model.costs.elapsedMilliseconds/1000).toFixed(2)} seconds wall time · ${(model.costs.cpuMilliseconds/1000).toFixed(2)} seconds process CPU · ${(model.costs.allocatedBytes/1000000).toFixed(1)} MB cumulatively allocated. ${model.metrics.length} compact episode records retained.`;
document.querySelector('#episodes').innerHTML=model.episodes.map(e=>`<article data-episode="${esc(e.id)}"><h3>${esc(e.title)}</h3><p class="meta">${esc(e.family)} · ${esc(names[e.policy]||e.policy)} · ${e.cells} cells · ${e.initialCompatible} initially compatible</p><div class="status ${e.identified?'':'open'}">${esc(e.status)}</div><div class="pictures"><figure>${e.beforeImage?`<a href="${esc(e.beforeImage)}"><img src="${esc(e.beforeImage)}" alt="Initial provisional sample for ${esc(e.id)}"></a>`:'<div class="empty">No admissible initial sample</div>'}<figcaption>Initial provisional sample · not an observation of the concealed source</figcaption></figure><figure>${e.afterImage?`<a href="${esc(e.afterImage)}"><img src="${esc(e.afterImage)}" alt="Final conditional sample for ${esc(e.id)}"></a>`:'<div class="empty">No single supported final output</div>'}<figcaption>Final selected sample after ${e.requests} requests · ${e.finalCompatible} compatible candidates remain</figcaption></figure></div><div class="steps">${e.steps.map((s,i)=>`<div class="step"><h4>${i+1}. Request ${esc(s.roles.join(' + '))}</h4><p>${s.before} → ${s.after} compatible candidates · observed replies: <code>${esc(s.words.join('; '))}</code></p><details><summary>Ranking inputs and retained evidence</summary><p>Normalized candidate disagreement ${s.features[1].toFixed(3)}; query overlap ${s.features[2].toFixed(3)}; offered role units ${s.features[3].toFixed(3)}; already known ${s.features[4].toFixed(3)}.</p><p>Learned score ${s.prediction.toFixed(4)} (a ranking score, not a probability). ${s.conflicts} same-event conflict witnesses remain.</p></details></div>`).join('')||'<p class="small">No evidence requests made.</p>'}</div><p class="small">${esc(e.evaluation)}</p></article>`).join('');
document.querySelector('#limits').innerHTML=model.limits.map(text=>`<li>${esc(text)}</li>`).join('');document.querySelector('#archive').textContent=`${model.nativeElements.toLocaleString()} retained native participants · ${model.auditOutputs} independently checked output executions · native archive restoration verified. ${model.incompleteGenericReaders} generic motif reads remain incomplete under their original budget. Full training outcomes and selected episodes are retained; other evaluation worlds are released.`;
</script></main></body></html>
""".Replace("__DATA__", data);
